        {"label": "b)", "expectedLatex": "2\\cdot3^{n-1}"}
      ],
      "domain": "Denominators 8 and 4*3^n never vanish; valid for integer n (and real n)."
    },
    {
      "exercise": "297",
      "derivation": "Over the reals, y=4*(x-5/8)^2+87/16, with minimum 87/16. For y=3 solve 4x^2-5x+4=0: discriminant 25-64=-39<0, no real x. For y=6 solve 4x^2-5x+1=0=(4x-1)*(x-1): x=1/4 or 1.",
      "parts": [
